  "rationale": "A wins with 98, ahead of C at 95 and B at 85. A is the only output that fully meets the velocity and projection criterion: it measures velocity in CSS px/s, gives a concrete projectedY formula with a 150ms horizon, keeps velocity handoff separate from snap selection, and uses an interruptible, critically damped settle. It also explicitly samples presentation position and velocity before cancelling an animation. C is close but less precise about units and the projection horizon. B lacks velocity handoff into the settle and any projected endpoint, which costs it points on interruption and velocity.",
